      "title": "At a glance",
      "body": "For travelers, Cho tôi hóa đơn is the phrase to keep ready for \"Please give me the receipt\" in buying small items, receipts, bags, and everyday errands. Use this after paying when you still need the receipt. It works best when you focus on putting the need first and leaving room for the helper to confirm the detail. After you say it, listen for a confirmation, a handoff, a price, or a follow-up question; the next rows help you keep the exchange moving.",
